  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "When ingame and using the PSVR2 controllers, only a limited set of gestures are available. Examples:\n\n- When thumbs are resting on the controller buttons, they are considered raised. This means that \"thumbsup\" is accessible but \"fist\" is not. Also, \"handgun\" is accessible but \"fingerpoint\" is not. (Edit: Resting the thumb on the thumbstick does not count as having the thumb raised for gestures, but visually appears as having a raised thumb.)\n\n- When the index finger trigger is pressed but the grip is not touched, the hand tracking translates this to index finger and middle fingers being curled inwards. On Quest, this would map to \"rocknroll\".\n\n- When the index finger is raised from the trigger, there is no way to activate \"victory\"\n\nAs far as I know, PSVR2 controllers are similar to Meta Quest controllers and have most of the same sensors. \n\nThere are finger sensors on the face buttons, analogue stick, grip button, and trigger. The grip and trigger sensors can detect proximity too. \n\nThe design of the controller means your thumb naturally rests on the buttons. This is a little different from the Quest controllers which have a dedicated thumbrest area and sensor.\n\nThe grip is not an analogue button. If I remember correctly, the grip on the Quest controllers only has one sensor for the whole thing though. \n\nIt would be ideal to have full gesture support with the PSVR2 controllers, as there doesn't seem to be any missing functionality that would prevent it.",
